WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.681 --> 00:00:02.864
- [Narrator] It was a trial
that captivated a nation.

00:00:02.864 --> 00:00:03.697
- [Male News Anchor] Lorena Bobbitt.

00:00:03.697 --> 00:00:04.530
- [Female News Anchor] Lorena Bobbitt.

00:00:04.530 --> 00:00:05.363
- [Male News Anchor] Lorena Bobbitt.

00:00:05.363 --> 00:00:06.196
- Took a knife.

00:00:06.196 --> 00:00:07.459
- [News Announcer] Cut
off her husband's penis.

00:00:07.459 --> 00:00:08.536
- [Narrator] But what does Lorena Bobbitt

00:00:08.536 --> 00:00:10.597
have to do with this thing?

00:00:10.597 --> 00:00:11.430
(bubbling)

00:00:11.430 --> 00:00:14.013
(gentle music)

00:00:15.274 --> 00:00:17.006
Let's take a step back.

00:00:17.006 --> 00:00:18.832
This is the Bobbit worm.

00:00:18.832 --> 00:00:22.174
It's a species of Eunice, Euna--

00:00:22.174 --> 00:00:23.202
- [Man] Eunice.

00:00:23.202 --> 00:00:24.035
- [Narrator] Thanks, Terry.

00:00:24.035 --> 00:00:25.242
- [Terry] You're most welcome.

00:00:25.242 --> 00:00:27.000
- [Narrator] That's Dr. Terry Gosliner.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:28.755
- [Terry] T-E-R-R-Y, G-O-S--

00:00:28.755 --> 00:00:29.613
- [Man] He's a senior curator at

00:00:29.613 --> 00:00:31.618
the California Academy of Sciences.

00:00:31.618 --> 00:00:33.979
- [Terry] And I do research on coral reefs

00:00:33.979 --> 00:00:35.144
around the world.

00:00:35.144 --> 00:00:36.508
- [Narrator] He's the one
who gave the Bobbit worm

00:00:36.508 --> 00:00:37.341
its name.

00:00:37.341 --> 00:00:38.630
They go way back.

00:00:38.630 --> 00:00:41.598
- [Terry] In 1992, I
went to the Philippines,

00:00:41.598 --> 00:00:43.894
and I saw my first Bobbit worm.

00:00:43.894 --> 00:00:46.236
To actually see it in action was really

00:00:46.236 --> 00:00:48.944
one of the most amazing things I've seen.

00:00:48.944 --> 00:00:51.503
(lively music)

00:00:51.503 --> 00:00:53.086
- [Narrator] This thing has nope, nope, nope

00:00:53.086 --> 00:00:54.946
written all over it.

00:00:54.946 --> 00:00:56.300
- [Terry] I'm sorry, what?

00:00:56.300 --> 00:00:58.149
- [Narrator] From it's
spiked glowing exoskeleton.

00:00:58.149 --> 00:01:01.219
- [Terry] And the body is
very iridescent, shiny.

00:01:01.219 --> 00:01:03.167
- [Narrator] To its spring-loaded jaws.

00:01:03.167 --> 00:01:05.463
- [Terry] They just spring
shut, like a bear trap.

00:01:05.463 --> 00:01:06.940
- [Narrator] And its
unique predatory style.

00:01:06.940 --> 00:01:09.334
- [Terry] When it sees a
fish, it pops more and more

00:01:09.334 --> 00:01:12.123
out of the water, and then grabs the fish

00:01:12.123 --> 00:01:14.060
and takes it back into the sand.

00:01:14.060 --> 00:01:15.416
(people gasp)

00:01:15.416 --> 00:01:16.312
- [Woman] What?

00:01:16.312 --> 00:01:19.154
- [Narrator] Anyway,
after years of research

00:01:19.154 --> 00:01:22.304
in the Indo-Pacific, Dr.
Gosliner published this book.

00:01:22.304 --> 00:01:24.677
- [Terry] Coral Reef
Animals of the Indo-Pacific.

00:01:24.677 --> 00:01:26.313
- [Narrator] When it came
time to name the worm,

00:01:26.313 --> 00:01:29.583
Dr. Gosliner found an unlikely
source of inspiration.

00:01:29.583 --> 00:01:33.380
- [Terry] There was this guy
named John Wayne Bobbitt,

00:01:33.380 --> 00:01:37.524
who had cheated on his wife,
and while he was sleeping

00:01:37.524 --> 00:01:40.750
one night, she cut off
his penis and threw it

00:01:40.750 --> 00:01:42.844
in a field nearby.

00:01:42.844 --> 00:01:43.783
- [Narrator] Wait, what?

00:01:43.783 --> 00:01:44.616
And the worm?

00:01:44.616 --> 00:01:48.365
- [Terry] Basically the
ability to use his massive jaws

00:01:48.365 --> 00:01:52.532
to cut the spinal cord of
a fish was something that

00:01:53.506 --> 00:01:57.091
reminded me of what Lorena
Bobbitt did to her husband.

00:01:57.091 --> 00:01:57.924
- [Narrator] So there you have it.

00:01:57.924 --> 00:02:01.316
Something else to keep you up at night.

00:02:01.316 --> 00:02:02.719
- [Terry] I've never
had nightmares about it.

00:02:02.719 --> 00:02:05.969
- [Narrator] Yeah, whatever, Dr. Terry.

